<title>POLAND: Optimus to issue GDRs by end 1997.</title>
<headline>Optimus to issue GDRs by end 1997.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-07-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Polish computer maker Optimus SA plans to issue Global Depositary Receipts (GDRs) by the end of the year for some of its existing shares, the company's spokesman said on Thursday.</p>
<p>&quot;Optimus is preparing for an issue of GDRs which will take place by the end of the year. The issue of GDRs will be for existing company shares,&quot; Marek Macias told a news conference.</p>
<p>Macias said further details concerning the GDR issue would be given in early September.</p>
<p>Optimus currently has 6,484,108 shares outstanding.</p>
<p>-- Dorota Sekulska +48 22 653 9700</p>
